 "critic": "The strongest generated cues were interchangeable names, repeated full names, fixed rewards, shifts from third-person reporting into first-person speech, and recurring three-option menus followed by a reputation or stranger justification. Paying the victim's loss or covering an unrelated shift often felt inserted to supply another solution. The Friday fee cards repeated conspicuously, but their extortion pressure still felt plausible and local. The strongest hooks connected an action to a consequence: delaying a collector invites escalation, injury threatens income, and crew conflict threatens retaliation. Ivo's collective refusal and Linh's attacker taking nothing supplied details that made me want to learn what happened next.",
 "sheet": 3
